  "output_id": "o_508c33f830d4",
  "case": "Funders who might pay for Harborlight's sixth site will read this deck. They need to believe that demand is growing faster than five sites can handle, and that more money will bring more results. The strongest evidence: enrollment rose from 936 to 1,148, and 287 adults were still waiting at year end, most of them at Eastgate and Riverside. Also, 68% of learners who stayed at least 12 weeks gained a reading level, at $1,237 per learner. Funders will ask what the new site adds, what it costs and who pays for it today. The ask is $190,000 more a year: the gap between the FY2026 spending of $1,420,000 and the proposed FY2027 budget of $1,610,000. That pays for the Eastgate site and two site coordinators.",
